.TH CRC32TEST 1
.SH NAME
crc32test \- regression test for crc32(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crc32test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Crc32test
loads
.BR /p9/dis/crc32.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR runstring(args,\ input) ,
and checks it against golden output for the empty string, several short
strings, and both custom
.RB ( -i / -x )
and non-default
.RB ( -p )
parameters.
.PP
The default-parameter cases are checked against an independent oracle
\(em Python's
.B zlib.crc32
\(em which computes the same standard CRC-32 this program's own
defaults implement, but shares no code with this translation. The
custom-parameter case has no such off-the-shelf oracle, so it was
checked against a from-scratch Python re-implementation of
.BR crc32.c 's
own table-based algorithm (independent of this Limbo translation, not
derived from it) before being written down as a golden value.
.PP
Prints one line per failure to standard error, a final
.IR N " passed, " N " failed"
summary to standard output, and exits with a non-nil status if
anything failed.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/crc32test.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR crc32 (1)
.SH BUGS
Runs
.I crc32
in-process via its
.B runstring
seam, which only exercises the "read one input" path \(em not
.IR crc32 's
own
.BR init ,
argument-count handling, multiple real
.I file
arguments, or the per-file open/read failure bookkeeping (a failure on
one file not stopping the rest, reported only at the end), none of
which
.B runstring
goes through.
